author: pi-agent
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T04:43:54.917Z",pi-agent,"Bumped @unbrained/pm-cli devDependency to 2026.7.29, set peerDependency to >=2026.7.29. Audited for 'list --all' and 'list -a': no hits found. Upstream workaround audit: GH-651/672/785/792/794 - no hits. GH-676 (list --tag CSV) - two hits in index.ts comment and README.md showing pm list --tag with a single tag value (not CSV), just documentation of the cycle tag feature. No workarounds to remove."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T05:02:45.370Z",claude-orchestrator,"Orchestrator follow-up from Greptile review on pm-jira#48, applied fleet-wide after checking all 18 READMEs. The Requirements section still advertised a pm-cli floor of 2026.7.5 while peerDependencies now demands >=2026.7.29, which misleads installers and invites strict-peer install failures for versions the docs present as supported. Updated the floor to >=2026.7.29. Only three packages carried a stale requirement floor (pm-gantt-chart, pm-jira, pm-linear); the other pm-cli version references across the fleet are feature-availability notes such as the 2026.7.19 atomic-import and 2026.7.22 merge-reconcile lines, which remain historically accurate and were deliberately left alone."
close_reason: "Bumped @unbrained/pm-cli to 2026.7.29 (devDep + peerDep >=2026.7.29). No 'list --all' hits found. No upstream workarounds to remove. All quality gates pass: 63 tests, coverage lines 70.53% (threshold 70), branches 80.42% (threshold 80), functions 80.43% (threshold 80). Changelog check and audit:prod clean."
body: ""
